{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":18914,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"2bc5dd46-5787-5a4a-9aec-6a7b73ff2433","total_cost_usd":0.217894,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7027,"cache_read_input_tokens":905,"output_tokens":1454,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7027,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1454,"cache_read_input_tokens":905,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7027},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3664,"outputTokens":13,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.003729,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":1454,"cacheReadInputTokens":905,"cacheCreationInputTokens":7027,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.214165,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"declaration_consistent\":true,\"selected_report_demonstration\":\"issue\",\"lock_follows_declaration\":true,\"reasons\":[\"The declaration names plot_id as the independent-unit column, and the frozen data bear this out: each of KF-01..KF-06 appears exactly three times (once per survey round), each plot_id maps to exactly one treatment arm (KF-01..03 rewetted, KF-04..06 drained), and the data description states that rows sharing a plot_id are repeat visits to one collar whose readings resemble each other; no plot straddles both arms.\",\"The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it states there are 18 readings from only 6 chamber plots each visited on 3 survey rounds, then says 'Every reading in the file was entered as a separate observation in the test' and reports t(16) = 19.600 on all 18 readings via a row-independent two-sample Student t test, so repeated measurements from the same independent unit (plot) were treated as independent observations, with only 6 truly independent units (3 per arm) inflating the effective sample size and degrees of freedom.\",\"Because the issue is present and shown in the report itself, the selected result (p < 0.001, t(16)) is not supported at the declared unit of independence; a valid analysis would aggregate to per-plot means (n = 3 per arm, df = 4) or model the within-plot dependence.\",\"A lock was minted, and its unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone: authorized_key_columns is exactly ['plot_id'], matching the declared independent-unit column, scoped to the same input path/digest and to the scipy.stats.ttest_ind procedure record, with authority_limitations correctly disclaiming any claim about numerical impact or scientific correctness.\",\"Note the lock only authorizes the unit-key declaration; it does not and cannot legitimize entering all 18 dependent rows into ttest_ind, so the pseudoreplication finding stands independently of the lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["The declaration names plot_id as the independent-unit column, and the frozen data bear this out: each of KF-01..KF-06 appears exactly three times (once per survey round), each plot_id maps to exactly one treatment arm (KF-01..03 rewetted, KF-04..06 drained), and the data description states that rows sharing a plot_id are repeat visits to one collar whose readings resemble each other; no plot straddles both arms.","The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it states there are 18 readings from only 6 chamber plots each visited on 3 survey rounds, then says 'Every reading in the file was entered as a separate observation in the test' and reports t(16) = 19.600 on all 18 readings via a row-independent two-sample Student t test, so repeated measurements from the same independent unit (plot) were treated as independent observations, with only 6 truly independent units (3 per arm) inflating the effective sample size and degrees of freedom.","Because the issue is present and shown in the report itself, the selected result (p < 0.001, t(16)) is not supported at the declared unit of independence; a valid analysis would aggregate to per-plot means (n = 3 per arm, df = 4) or model the within-plot dependence.","A lock was minted, and its unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone: authorized_key_columns is exactly ['plot_id'], matching the declared independent-unit column, scoped to the same input path/digest and to the scipy.stats.ttest_ind procedure record, with authority_limitations correctly disclaiming any claim about numerical impact or scientific correctness.","Note the lock only authorizes the unit-key declaration; it does not and cannot legitimize entering all 18 dependent rows into ttest_ind, so the pseudoreplication finding stands independently of the lock."]},"ttft_ms":9544,"ttft_stream_ms":1504,"time_to_request_ms":9,"type":"result","duration_ms":17622,"uuid":"ce4ea609-5b81-4c33-a685-052854365a75"}
